<div class="py-12">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Landing Page Management
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-xl text-gray-500 sm:mt-4">
        View and manage your landing page variants for A/B testing and conversion optimization.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%= render 'shared/landing_pages_list' %>
    
    <div class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Landing Page Performance</h2>
      
      <div class="bg-white shadow rounded-lg p-6">
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
          Use PostHog to create funnels and analyze conversion rates for each landing page variant.
          Below are some key metrics you can track:
        </p>
        
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-8">
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Visitor to Lead Rate</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
              Percentage of visitors who submit the initial email capture form.
              <br><br>
              <span class="block mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600">
                PostHog event: "initial_email_capture_click"
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Lead to Completion Rate</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
              Percentage of leads who complete the full lead capture process.
              <br><br>
              <span class="block mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600">
                PostHog event: "lead_form_complete_click"
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">UTM Source Analysis</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
              Compare which traffic sources perform best with each landing page variant.
              <br><br>
              <span class="block mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600">
                PostHog property: "source"
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Integration Guide</h2>
      
      <div class="bg-white shadow rounded-lg p-6">
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
          Use these UTM parameters with your marketing campaigns to track performance:
        </p>
        
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <pre class="text-sm text-gray-800">https://yourdomain.com/landing_pages/cfo?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=cfo_targeting&utm_content=ad1</pre>
        </div>
        
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Recommended UTM Parameters:</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-600 mb-6">
          <li><strong>utm_source</strong>: The platform where your link is placed (google, facebook, linkedin, email)</li>
          <li><strong>utm_medium</strong>: The marketing medium (cpc, email, social, banner)</li>
          <li><strong>utm_campaign</strong>: The specific campaign name (spring_sale, product_launch)</li>
          <li><strong>utm_content</strong>: Used to differentiate similar content (button, image, text_link)</li>
          <li><strong>utm_term</strong>: Used for paid search keywords</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 text-sm text-blue-800">
          <p class="font-semibold">Pro Tip:</p>
          <p>Create campaign links with these formats for consistency:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2">
            <li>CFO targeting: <code>/landing_pages/cfo?utm_source=SOURCE&utm_medium=MEDIUM&utm_campaign=cfo_targeting</code></li>
            <li>Small business: <code>/landing_pages/small_business?utm_source=SOURCE&utm_medium=MEDIUM&utm_campaign=smb_targeting</code></li>
            <li>QuickBooks users: <code>/landing_pages/quickbooks?utm_source=SOURCE&utm_medium=MEDIUM&utm_campaign=qbo_targeting</code></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>